From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:56:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb+LibWebView+WebContent: Let the embedder's pages use
 the clipboard

Browsers let an extension's pages use the clipboard from script, with
no user activation, if the extension has the clipboardRead and
clipboardWrite permissions. Password managers rely on it to clear what
they copied a while later: Proton Pass's offscreen document pastes to
see whether the clipboard still holds what it copied, and if so, copies
over it.

A URLSchemeBridge can now say whether each of its scheme's documents
may read or write the clipboard this way. One that may write can copy
and cut with execCommand(). One that may read can paste with
execCommand("paste"), which pastes synchronously, as in other browsers,
so that the pasted content is there when execCommand() returns. No
other document can paste from script, as before.

The renderer asks the UI process about a document of an embedder scheme
when it has no activation to go on. The UI process answers from its own
records of the document, never from the renderer's, and lets a page
without activation write the clipboard only if it hosts such a document.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
